import Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic
/-! An independent reader transcribed, from the typeset page image only, the y-redshift distance coefficients printed in K. Bamba, S. Capozziello, S. Nojiri, S. D. Odintsov, "Dark energy cosmology: the equivalent description via different theoretical models and cosmography tests" (2012), arXiv:1205.3421, version 3 (downloaded PDF). Equations read: (10.54) to (10.57) for the luminosity-distance coefficients with upper indices 2, 3, 4, and (10.61) to (10.63) for the angular-diameter-distance coefficients with upper indices 3 and 4. All coefficients are kept exactly as printed, with no corrections. -/
namespace Checked.Trust.SecondReading
/-- Bamba, Capozziello, Nojiri, Odintsov, arXiv:1205.3421v3, Eq. (10.54), PDF page 111 (printed page number 111). Symbol: D with upper index 2 and lower index L,y. It is the coefficient of y squared in the series of the luminosity distance in the y-redshift y = z/(1+z), written in terms of the deceleration parameter q (q₀), the jerk j (j₀) and the curvature parameter Ω (Ω₀ as the paper defines it). Printed as −(1/6)(12 − 5q₀ + 3q₀² − j₀ − Ω₀) on one line. No reading difficulty. -/
noncomputable def bamba12PrintedDL2y (q j Ω : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  -(1 / 6) * (12 - 5 * q + 3 * q ^ 2 - j - Ω)
/-- Bamba, Capozziello, Nojiri, Odintsov, arXiv:1205.3421v3, Eq. (10.55), PDF page 111 (printed page number 111). Symbol: D with upper index 3 and lower index L,y. It is the coefficient of y cubed in the y-redshift series of the luminosity distance, in terms of q (q₀), j (j₀), the snap s (s₀) and Ω (Ω₀). Printed as (1/24)[52 − 20q₀ + 21q₀² − 15q₀³ − 7j₀ + 10q₀j₀ + s₀ − 2Ω₀(1 + 3q₀)] on one line. No reading difficulty. -/
noncomputable def bamba12PrintedDL3y (q j s Ω : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  (1 / 24) * (52 - 20 * q + 21 * q ^ 2 - 15 * q ^ 3 - 7 * j + 10 * q * j + s - 2 * Ω * (1 + 3 * q))
/-- Bamba, Capozziello, Nojiri, Odintsov, arXiv:1205.3421v3, Eqs. (10.56) and (10.57), PDF page 111 (printed page number 111). Symbol: D with upper index 4 and lower index L,y. It is the coefficient of y to the fourth in the y-redshift series of the luminosity distance, in terms of q (q₀), j (j₀), s (s₀), the lerk l (l₀) and Ω (Ω₀). Printed as (1/120)[ ... ] over two lines. Reading choices: the first line ends with a plus sign after −15q₀s₀ and the second line begins with a minus sign before 57j₀, so two signs stand side by side across the line break; I read them as a plus followed by a minus, which is the sum of the first line and a negated 57 j₀. The term printed as 10j² has no subscript on j; I read it as 10 times the square of j₀ and used the argument j. Suspected misprint: the doubled sign at the line break and the missing subscript on j² look like typesetting artifacts, but nothing was corrected. -/
noncomputable def bamba12PrintedDL4y (q j s l Ω : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  (1 / 120) * (359 - 184 * q + 186 * q ^ 2 - 135 * q ^ 3 + 105 * q ^ 4 + 90 * q * j - 105 * q ^ 2 * j - 15 * q * s + -(57 * j) + 10 * j ^ 2 + 9 * s - l - 5 * Ω * (17 - 6 * q + 9 * q ^ 2 - 2 * j))
/-- Bamba, Capozziello, Nojiri, Odintsov, arXiv:1205.3421v3, Eq. (10.61), PDF page 111 (printed page number 111). Symbol: D with upper index 3 and lower index A,y. It is the coefficient of y cubed in the y-redshift series of the angular diameter distance, in terms of q (q₀), j (j₀), s (s₀) and Ω (Ω₀). Printed as −(1/24)(−2q₀ + 3q₀² + 15q₀³ − j₀ − 10q₀j₀ − s₀ + 2Ω₀) on one line. No reading difficulty. -/
noncomputable def bamba12PrintedDA3y (q j s Ω : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  -(1 / 24) * (-2 * q + 3 * q ^ 2 + 15 * q ^ 3 - j - 10 * q * j - s + 2 * Ω)
/-- Bamba, Capozziello, Nojiri, Odintsov, arXiv:1205.3421v3, Eqs. (10.62) and (10.63), PDF page 111 (printed page number 111). Symbol: D with upper index 4 and lower index A,y. It is the coefficient of y to the fourth in the y-redshift series of the angular diameter distance, in terms of q (q₀), j (j₀), s (s₀), l (l₀) and Ω (Ω₀). Printed as −(1/120)( ... ) over two lines. Reading choices: the first line ends with a plus sign after 15q₀s₀ and the second line begins with a minus sign before 3j₀, so two signs stand side by side across the line break; I read them as a plus followed by a minus. The term printed as 10j² has no subscript on j; I read it as 10 times the square of j₀ and used the argument j. Nothing was corrected. -/
noncomputable def bamba12PrintedDA4y (q j s l Ω : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  -(1 / 120) * (1 - 6 * q + 9 * q ^ 2 - 15 * q ^ 3 - 105 * q ^ 4 + 10 * q * j + 105 * q ^ 2 * j + 15 * q * s + -(3 * j) - 10 * j ^ 2 + s + l + 5 * Ω)
end Checked.Trust.SecondReading
